  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>Designed by a weapons manufacturer called Systech, this weapon is awkward and difficult to wield without special training. Shaped like a pistol with auxiliary sonic emitters attached to either side of the barrel, the Aurial Blaster can deafen a target with a successful hit. </p><p>When a target is struck by an Aurial Blaster, if the attack roll equals or exceeds the target's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fortitude_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fortitude Defense\">Fortitude Defense</a>, the target takes a -5 penalty on all <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> checks made until the end of the attacker's next turn. An Aurial Blaster is treated as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistol\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pistol\">Pistol</a> for the purpose of determining <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p><p>An Aurial Blaster requires a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>. After 50 shots, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> must be replaced. </p>",
